```
2025-10-27T14:05:53.148+10:00: Timed out waiting for device query: The wait operation timed out. (Code 0x00000102)
2025-10-27T14:05:53.148+10:00: Failed to setup adapter (problem code: 0x38, ntstatus: 0x0): The device is not ready for use. (Code 0x000010DF)
```

A common cause of this error code is a third-party component, such as an [NDIS Notify Object](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/network/about-notify-objects), that was previously installed but improperly removed. For example, some users have encountered this issue after deleting VMware Workstation from `%programfiles%` instead of properly uninstalling it, or after installing it on a removable drive and then disconnecting it. In cases like this, certain files remain registered with the OS, and it fails installing or configuring network adapters due to a missing file.

The script below can help identify certain missing components:
```ps1
$keyPaths = "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Network\*\*"
$keys = Get-ChildItem -Path $keyPaths -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
foreach ($key in $keys) {
     $ndiKeyPath = $key.PSPath + "\NDI"
     $clsid = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $ndiKeyPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).CLSID
     if ($null -ne $clsid) {
         $componentId = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $key.PSPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).ComponentId

         # Determine the path to the In-Proc COM Server .DLL
         $dllpath = ""
         try {
             $inprocServer32path = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Classes\CLSID\$clsid\InprocServer32"
             $dllpath = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $inprocServer32path)."(Default)"
         } catch {
             Write-Output "WARNING: The DLL registration not found for $clsid ($componentId)"
             continue
         }

         # Check if the path exists
         if (Test-Path -Path $dllpath) {
             Write-Output "Found the DLL for $clsid ($componentId) at $dllpath"
         } else {
             Write-Output "WARNING: The DLL for $clsid ($componentId) does not exist at $dllpath"
         }
     }
}
```
